    <h1>About SocialCareKit</h1>
    <p class="lead">SocialCareKit exists because the people doing the most important work in social care are usually the last to get good tools.</p>
    <p>Frontline staff in children's homes and adult services navigate a maze of regulations, acronyms and paperwork — often on their phone, mid-shift, at 3am. Registered managers rebuild the same templates from scratch in every new service. Workers wonder whether their sleep-in pay is legal and have nowhere quick to check.</p>
    <p>So we built a kit:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Interactive tools</strong> that answer real questions — pay, holiday, working time, notifications — instantly and privately. Everything runs in your browser; nothing you type reaches our servers.</li>
      <li><strong>A template library</strong> of properly structured documents mapped to the regulations they support, free to use within your organisation.</li>
      <li><strong>Plain-English guides</strong> to the law and practice frameworks that shape every shift.</li>
      <li><strong>A staff rights section</strong>, because a workforce that knows its rights is a safer workforce for the people it supports.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Who is behind this?</h2>
    <p>SocialCareKit is built and maintained by people with direct experience of the UK social care sector, with content reviewed on a rolling schedule — every tool and template shows its last-reviewed date, and you can <a href="/report-error/">report an error</a> on any page.</p>
    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>We are not affiliated with, or endorsed by, Ofsted, the Care Quality Commission, or any local authority. Everything here is guidance to support your professional judgement and your organisation's policies — not a replacement for either, and not legal advice.</p>
    <p><a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a> — suggestions for new tools and templates shape what we build next.</p>
